glog
------------------------------------------
The glog library implements application-level logging. This library provides
logging APIs based on C++-style streams and various helper macros.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgflags2.2-2.2.2-1
  libglog-devel-0.7.1-1bl2
  libglog2-0.7.1-1bl2
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libunwind1-22.1.8-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libgflags-devel-2.2.2-1
  libunwind-devel-22.1.8-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/google/glog

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/google/glog/archive/refs/tags/v0.7.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack glog-0.7.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./glog-0.7.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/glog-0.7.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/glog-0.7.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libglog2-0.7.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libglog-devel-0.7.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(glog)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/glog.README
  /usr/share/doc/glog/AUTHORS
  /usr/share/doc/glog/CONTRIBUTORS
  /usr/share/doc/glog/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/glog/ChangeLog
  /usr/share/doc/glog/README.rst

(libglog2)
  /usr/bin/cygglog-2.dll

(libglog-devel)
  /usr/include/glog/export.h
  /usr/include/glog/flags.h
  /usr/include/glog/log_severity.h
  /usr/include/glog/logging.h
  /usr/include/glog/platform.h
  /usr/include/glog/raw_logging.h
  /usr/include/glog/stl_logging.h
  /usr/include/glog/types.h
  /usr/include/glog/vlog_is_on.h
  /usr/lib/cmake/glog/glog-config-version.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/glog/glog-config.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/glog/glog-modules.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/glog/glog-targets-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/glog/glog-targets.cmake
  /usr/lib/libglog.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/libglog.pc

